C-side co-simulation tests (docs/VAMOS_AMS_DESIGN.md §7 P1-P7, §9 "C-side").

run_cside.py      the runner and the case list (python3 run_cside.py --help);
                  tests/vamos/test_cside_engine.py wraps it, one test per case
                  and engine
cside.vhd         the digital halves (VHDL-2008, real-valued boundary signals)
*.sim / *.cir     VACASK / Xyce decks (rc, rc2, sense07, senseramp, a2d,
                  fail.sim, a2dfail.cir, rc_nope); the stop_time_*, finish_*
                  and interrupt_running cases write rc with another stop (2 us
                  to 3 ms) into their run directory, finish_a2d_at_candidate a
                  slow divider deck, the ramp_* cases a divider deck with the
                  .tran line under test
*.boundary        boundary files (q: default ramps; q_r11: 10 ps; q_r0:
                  rise=0 clamped; q_rev: 10 ps rise / 1 ns fall; q2; ain; a2d)
stub_bridge.c     an old libcosim_bridge.so (no cosim_bridge_abi, or ABI 1)
stub_engine.c     a stand-in engine C interface: no <engine>_cosim_abi, or
                  ABI 2 with STUB_MODE=stall|fail|complete for nvc's run loop,
                  sigint_init|sigint_run for an interrupt in it
xyce_abi_shim.c   TEST ONLY: adds xyce_cosim_abi to a Xyce without the cosim
                  patches (--xyce-shim; the finish cases are then skipped)

Typical runs (WSL):
  python3 run_cside.py                                   # the default nvc build ($NVCB), both engines
  python3 run_cside.py --nvc-build DIR --engines vacask -k finish   # another nvc build tree
  python3 run_cside.py --engines xyce --xyce-shim        # before the Xyce patches
  python3 run_cside.py --old-bridge OLD.so --old-vacask OLDCI.so   # real old libraries
  python3 run_cside.py -k stop_time       # --stop-time counts of 2^32 fs and more (§6)
  python3 run_cside.py -k finish_10 -k finish_ms -k finish_a2d_at   # exact end-line times
  python3 run_cside.py -k ramp_late -k ramp_1p5s -k ramp_below      # P3 late in a run
  python3 run_cside.py -k interrupt       # SIGINT: "co-simulation interrupted at", exit 130
